    <!-- ============================================================
         Session E: real Fuel-sourced props (session A's structural
         blockout populated with detail). Every placement below was
         checked two ways before being written, not eyeballed:
         (1) exact-footprint overlap against every existing model's
             real pose/size (no unintended collisions, 0.3 m margin);
         (2) distance from every one of 1197 real ground-truth points
             logged across all 4 saved verification runs (2 clean
             unloaded round trips + the loaded round trip's two
             stages) - minimum clearance to any prop is 2.0 m against
             a 1.5 m safety buffer. See docs/construction_site_design.md
             for the Fuel model sourcing and validation/phase8/
             construction_site_descent/README.md for the full
             placement-verification method and the reverification
             results after adding these. -->

    <!-- Perimeter fencing + access-road traffic control (fence x2,
         Construction Cone x3, Speed limit sign) REMOVED here and
         staying removed - PERMANENTLY, not pending further work. Full
         history: originally margined (2.0-3.1 m clearance) against the
         worst leg-4 drift observed before the flat_mode crosstrack fix
         (up to 5.9-11.26 m). That fix (flat_mode's path_align_offset,
         see ramp_mppi_params.yaml) correctly shrank leg-4 drift on
         average, but a live post-fix reverification hit gate_cone_2
         directly (0.58 m clearance, the same wheels-spinning/chassis-
         frozen signature as the elevated-level seam bug) - 2 data
         points at the time, not enough to characterize a real bound,
         so the props were pulled rather than re-margined off a guess.

         CLOSED with a real distribution, not reopened as a guess:
         a follow-up session ran 8 independent loaded trials and 8
         independent unloaded attempts of the leg-4 return leg (fresh
         `ros2 launch` + fresh sim per trial, ground-truth polling via
         `gz topic`, ~450-1040 s each). Loaded leg-4 drift (the binding
         case - unloaded drift is much smaller): n=8, min=0.526 m,
         max=2.535 m, mean=1.263 m, sample stdev=0.695 m - CONVERGED
         (min/max/range stable from n=6 onward, not still swinging
         run to run; see the full running-stats table in validation/
         phase8/construction_site_descent/README.md's "Drift
         characterization" section) but inherently WIDE (range 2.0 m,
         ~5x spread between smallest and largest observed trial).
         Unloaded: n=4 valid (min=-0.203 m, max=0.005 m, mean=-0.102 m,
         stdev=0.101 m, tightly clustered). CAVEAT: these drift trials
         were collected while the trial harness was leaking stale ROS/
         gz processes (host load average 71-76 on 12 cores); the
         "stalled arc-turn" rate first recorded here did not reproduce
         on a clean host (see "Leg-3 completion recheck" in validation/
         phase8/construction_site_descent/README.md) and the drift
         distribution has NOT yet been re-collected on a clean host.

         Applying this project's own established margining convention
         (max relevant excursion + 1.5 m safety buffer, the same
         formula the laydown-area props elsewhere in this file are
         sized against): required clearance = 2.535 + 1.5 = 4.035 m
         from the leg-4 path centerline (Y=0). access_road is only
         6.1 m wide (Y in [-3.05, 3.05]; see its own <model> above) -
         its own half-width (3.05 m) is LESS than the required
         clearance, so no position within the drivable road corridor
         can satisfy it. There is no fixed placement for gate/access-
         road props that this data supports, converged distribution or
         not - the distribution characterizes the risk precisely enough
         to show why this area is a genuine standing limitation, not an
         open question. Laydown/office/waste-pad props (all well
         outside leg 4's observed or plausible reach, per the separate
         1197-point clearance check elsewhere in this file) are
         unaffected and stay in place. See "Drift characterization" in
         validation/phase8/construction_site_descent/README.md for
         every trial's raw data and the full margin derivation. -->

    <!-- Laydown area: palletized/stacked material, delivery-to-point-
         -of-use flow along +X (toward the ramp) - loose incoming
         pallets nearest the gate/delivery end, staged crates mid-yard,
         a ready-to-move pallet rack section nearest the ramp. All on
         laydown_area's top surface (0.1500 m after the fix) and all
         confined to Y in [2.5, 4.7] - clear of the full-width
         laydown_area (Y in [-5,5]) but, more importantly, clear of
         every one of the 1197 logged ground-truth points from every
         saved verification run (2.45-3.36 m minimum clearance),
         including the one loaded run whose return leg (open-loop,
         uncorrected heading from the arc-turn) drifted to Y=-5.92 m -
         see the "still-open finding" this margin was sized against in
         validation/phase8/construction_site_descent/README.md. -->
